flowchart TB
  accTitle: Commitment policy and reconsideration schedule are separate axes
  accDescr: The left axis defines when the intention is released: blind, single-minded, or open-minded. The right axis defines when the current course is reviewed: bold, cautious, intermediate, or event-sensitive. A system selects one policy and one schedule rather than choosing one value from a combined list.
  subgraph A[Axis 1: release condition]
    direction TB
    A1[Blind: retain until believed achieved]
    A2[Single-minded: achieved or believed impossible]
    A3[Open-minded: achieved or no longer desired]
  end
  subgraph B[Axis 2: review cadence]
    direction TB
    B1[Bold: after current plan]
    B2[Cautious: after each step]
    B3[Intermediate: bounded step interval]
    B4[Event-sensitive: relevant validated event]
  end
  A1 --- C[Choose independently]
  A2 --- C
  A3 --- C
  C --- B1
  C --- B2
  C --- B3
  C --- B4
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class A1,A2,A3 source
  class B1,B2,B3,B4 output
  class C process
